# Commit changes for every prompt

After completing any task or prompt in this project, commit the resulting changes
to git. Do not leave work uncommitted at the end of a turn.

- Stage only the files relevant to the task (`git add <paths>`), never blanket
  `git add -A` unless the whole workspace is confirmed to belong to the task.
- Write a concise, descriptive commit message that explains *what* changed and
  *why* (e.g. `feat(pos): add barcode-first billing screen`).
- If there is nothing to commit (for example a read-only question), say so
  explicitly instead of making an empty commit.
- Do not push, open PRs, or modify remotes unless the user asks for that too.
- Verify the commit with `git status --short` and include the short SHA in the
  final response.
